  "notes": "{和|やわ}らぐ expresses the softening or easing of something intense, harsh, or tense.\n\nVERB TYPE:\n- Godan verb (ぐ-verb)\n- Intransitive\n- Transitive pair: {和|やわ}らげる\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みが{和|やわ}らぐ (pain eases)\n- {緊張|きんちょう}が{和|やわ}らぐ (tension eases)\n- {表情|ひょうじょう}が{和|やわ}らぐ (expression softens)\n- {寒|さむ}さが{和|やわ}らぐ (cold eases)\n- {怒|いか}りが{和|やわ}らぐ (anger subsides)\n- {気持|きも}ちが{和|やわ}らぐ (feelings calm down)\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {和|やわ}らぐ (intransitive): The pain eases on its own\n- {和|やわ}らげる (transitive): Someone eases/softens something\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {和|やわ}らげる (transitive: to ease, soften)\n- {落|お}ち{着|つ}く (to calm down)\n- {収|おさ}まる (to subside)\n- {緩|ゆる}む (to loosen, relax)\n\nREGISTER: Neutral to slightly formal. Common in everyday use.",
